    "created_at": "2016-05-17T22:33:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-17T22:33:59Z",
    "body": "I think some UA's may also treat it as prefetch.. And one could imagine that the UA might just want to do a preconnect if its not willing to fetch _any_ data - e.g. when in a data savings mode, or some such. \n\nWould it make sense to relax the language and define rel=next as a ~general resource hints signal, allowing the UA to determine which type (if any) it wants to use for that particular resource? \n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
